{"archetypes":[{"name":"fd-chain-tracer","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's correctness hinges on accurately identifying which scopes have FD 2 redirected to files vs. available for chat; a misclassification means tails are silently captured rather than surfaced.","prompt_body":"Trace the complete FD inheritance chain for each lane the plan modifies (codex-implement, cursor-implement, lint-fix run_codex, lint-fix run_cursor, ship-pr fix-loop, ship-pr recovery waterfall, step5 loop) and verify the plan's assertion about where emit_failed_agent_stderr_tail_larch_err must be called (caller scope vs. in-loop) matches the actual FD routing in the cited script files. Identify any lane where the plan places an emit call inside a subprocess or redirect scope where FD 2, FD 3, or FD 4 under quiet mode would be captured to a file rather than reaching chat. Check whether the plan's 'do not call emit inside subprocesses whose FD 2 was redirected' guidance is consistently applied to every emit site proposed across all modified scripts, including the step5 loop's set -e-restored scope and the run_lint_fix_loop_capture 2>\"$fail_file\" redirect. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"kv-caller-contract","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan introduces new KV fields and changes run_cursor exit-code propagation semantics; any existing caller that assumes the old return behavior or does not parse the new KV could silently break without being flagged by the plan.","prompt_body":"Enumerate every new or changed stdout contract the plan introduces: the STDERR_TAIL_PATH= KV emitted by lint-fix-loop.sh, the run_cursor exit-code propagation change from always-0 to mirroring run_codex, and the _surface_lint_fix_stderr_tail parsing logic in ship-pr.sh. For each contract change, identify all current callers in the scope files and broader codebase (run_lint_fix_loop_capture, step5 loop, _rcc_handle_fix_status sites, and any other lint-fix invoker) and verify the plan explicitly accounts for each caller. Check whether the plan's backward-compatibility claim holds: confirm no caller assumes run_cursor currently returns 0 on all paths, and verify the parse-before-rm ordering for STDERR_TAIL_PATH inside step5_parse_lint_capture_file is the only consumption point so that the immediately following rm -f cannot lose the stem before terminal case arms call step5_surface_lint_stderr_tail. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
